<thead><tr><th>Audience state</th><th>Required handling</th><th>Why it matters</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>No documented consent</td><td>Hold all flash sales marketing; transactional only</td><td>Every flash sales send stands on documented consent</td></tr>
<tr><td>Consented, never purchased</td><td>Open flash sales with guidance and proof, not discounts</td><td>Flash Sales margin suffers when discounts arrive first</td></tr>
<tr><td>Active cart, no checkout</td><td>Flash Sales reminder with product context; discount withheld</td><td>Protects flash sales profit when purchase intent is hottest</td></tr>
<tr><td>Purchased recently</td><td>Flash Sales buyers get education, not another pitch</td><td>Flash Sales suppression protects the new-customer glow</td></tr>
<tr><td>Refund or return open</td><td>No flash sales promos mid-case; resume after resolution</td><td>Service-active flash sales shoppers reject promos</td></tr>
<tr><td>Repeated non-engagement</td><td>Flash Sales sunset policy precedes complaint spikes</td><td>Flash Sales inboxing survives on timely sunsets</td></tr>
<tr><td>SMS consent present</td><td>Hold flash sales texts to quiet hours and frequency limits</td><td>Flash Sales SMS risk exceeds email per complaint</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wholesale or B2B account</td><td>Isolate flash sales wholesale comms from retail blasts</td><td>Wholesale flash sales terms forbid retail-style offers</td></tr>
<tr><td>Free or disposable email domain</td><td>Verify flash sales throwaway addresses pre-journey</td><td>Unverified flash sales addresses poison sender score</td></tr>
<tr><td>Staff and test accounts</td><td>Strip flash sales test data from live journeys</td><td>Internal flash sales activity corrupts program metrics</td></tr>
<tr><td>Competitor or researcher signals</td><td>Treat flash sales snoops under normal consent policy</td><td>Flash Sales one-offs breed audit gaps</td></tr>
<tr><td>Legacy list without timestamps</td><td>Re-permission legacy flash sales lists pre-automation</td><td>Timestamp-less flash sales consent is legal exposure</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
